<%#
  The full-pane note (PRD §7.7) — what a sidebar row opens.

  The third wrapper around `notes/_fields`, and the cheapest possible version
  of §8.4: the same fields, the same autosave controller mounted unchanged,
  a different frame. If this file had needed the field partial edited to work,
  milestone 3's split would have been wrong.

  There is no Done button. Leaving is navigating away, and autosave already
  flushes on `turbo:before-visit` and on unload — a button here would be a
  second way to do what the back link does, and the one thing §8.1 forbids is
  a save button.
%>
<% content_for :title, "#{@note.tree_label} — notbuk" %>

<main class="pane">
  <%# Back to whatever board was underneath: the folder's if the note is in
      one, otherwise all notes. %>
  <%= link_to pane_back_path(@note), class: "pane__back" do %>
    ← <%= @note.folder&.name || "Notes" %>
  <% end %>

  <div class="pane__sheet"
       data-controller="pane autosave"
       data-autosave-create-url-value="<%= notes_path %>"
       data-autosave-url-value="<%= note_path(@note) %>"
       data-action="submit->pane#preventSubmit
                    input->autosave#schedule
                    change->autosave#saveNow
                    focusout->autosave#saveNow">
    <%= render "notes/fields", note: @note, folders: @folders %>
  </div>
</main>
